@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Transaction with TRY...CATCH";
}

<div class="container-fluid py-4">

    <!-- =========================
         PAGE HEADER
    ========================== -->

    <div class="mb-4">

        <h1 class="fw-bold text-primary">
            Transaction with TRY...CATCH
        </h1>

        <p class="text-muted fs-5">
            Learn how TRY...CATCH can be used with SQL Server
            Transactions to handle errors and safely commit or
            roll back database changes.
        </p>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         WHAT IS TRY...CATCH?
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                What is TRY...CATCH?
            </h2>

            <p>
                <strong>TRY...CATCH</strong> is used in SQL Server
                to handle errors that occur while executing SQL statements.
            </p>

            <p>
                The statements that may generate an error are placed
                inside the <strong>TRY</strong> block. If an error occurs,
                SQL Server transfers control to the <strong>CATCH</strong>
                block.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         BASIC SYNTAX
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Basic TRY...CATCH Syntax
            </h2>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>BEGIN TRY

    -- SQL statements

END TRY

BEGIN CATCH

    -- Error handling

END CATCH;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         TRANSACTION WITH TRY CATCH
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Transaction with TRY...CATCH
            </h2>

            <p>
                A transaction can be combined with TRY...CATCH so that
                successful operations are committed and failed operations
                are rolled back.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>BEGIN TRY

    BEGIN TRANSACTION;

    -- SQL statements

    COMMIT TRANSACTION;

END TRY

BEGIN CATCH

    ROLLBACK TRANSACTION;

END CATCH;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         SIMPLE EXAMPLE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Simple Example
            </h2>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>BEGIN TRY

    BEGIN TRANSACTION;

    INSERT INTO Students
    (
        StudentId,
        StudentName,
        City,
        Age
    )
    VALUES
    (
        501,
        'Rahul',
        'Pune',
        22
    );

    COMMIT TRANSACTION;

END TRY

BEGIN CATCH

    ROLLBACK TRANSACTION;

END CATCH;</code></pre>

            <p class="mt-3">
                If the INSERT operation succeeds, the transaction
                is committed. If an error occurs, the CATCH block
                executes and the transaction is rolled back.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         ERROR MESSAGE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Handling the Error Message
            </h2>

            <p>
                SQL Server provides functions that can be used inside
                the CATCH block to retrieve information about an error.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>BEGIN TRY

    BEGIN TRANSACTION;

    -- SQL statements

    COMMIT TRANSACTION;

END TRY

BEGIN CATCH

    IF @@TRANCOUNT &gt; 0
        ROLLBACK TRANSACTION;

    SELECT
        ERROR_NUMBER() AS ErrorNumber,
        ERROR_MESSAGE() AS ErrorMessage,
        ERROR_LINE() AS ErrorLine;

END CATCH;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         IMPORTANT ERROR FUNCTIONS
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Important Error Functions
            </h2>

            <div class="table-responsive">

                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                    <thead class="table-primary">

                        <tr>

                            <th>Function</th>

                            <th>Purpose</th>

                        </tr>

                    </thead>

                    <tbody>

                        <tr>

                            <td>
                                <code>ERROR_NUMBER()</code>
                            </td>

                            <td>
                                Returns the error number.
                            </td>

                        </tr>

                        <tr>

                            <td>
                                <code>ERROR_MESSAGE()</code>
                            </td>

                            <td>
                                Returns the error message.
                            </td>

                        </tr>

                        <tr>

                            <td>
                                <code>ERROR_LINE()</code>
                            </td>

                            <td>
                                Returns the line number where the error occurred.
                            </td>

                        </tr>

                        <tr>

                            <td>
                                <code>ERROR_PROCEDURE()</code>
                            </td>

                            <td>
                                Returns the name of the stored procedure
                                where the error occurred, when applicable.
                            </td>

                        </tr>

                        <tr>

                            <td>
                                <code>ERROR_SEVERITY()</code>
                            </td>

                            <td>
                                Returns the severity level of the error.
                            </td>

                        </tr>

                        <tr>

                            <td>
                                <code>ERROR_STATE()</code>
                            </td>

                            <td>
                                Returns the state number of the error.
                            </td>

                        </tr>

                    </tbody>

                </table>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         WHY CHECK @@TRANCOUNT?
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Why Check @@TRANCOUNT?
            </h2>

            <p>
                <strong>@@TRANCOUNT</strong> returns the number of
                active transactions for the current session.
            </p>

            <p>
                Before executing ROLLBACK TRANSACTION in the CATCH
                block, it is useful to check whether a transaction
                is currently active.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>IF @@TRANCOUNT &gt; 0
    ROLLBACK TRANSACTION;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         COMPLETE EXAMPLE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Complete Transaction Example
            </h2>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>BEGIN TRY

    BEGIN TRANSACTION;

    INSERT INTO Students
    (
        StudentId,
        StudentName,
        City,
        Age
    )
    VALUES
    (
        502,
        'Priya',
        'Mumbai',
        21
    );

    UPDATE Students
    SET Age = Age + 1
    WHERE StudentId = 502;

    COMMIT TRANSACTION;

    PRINT 'Transaction completed successfully.';

END TRY

BEGIN CATCH

    IF @@TRANCOUNT &gt; 0
        ROLLBACK TRANSACTION;

    SELECT
        ERROR_NUMBER() AS ErrorNumber,
        ERROR_MESSAGE() AS ErrorMessage,
        ERROR_LINE() AS ErrorLine;

END CATCH;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         TRANSACTION FLOW
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Transaction with TRY...CATCH Flow
            </h2>

            <div class="alert alert-primary">

                <strong>Step 1:</strong>
                Start TRY block.

                <br /><br />

                ↓

                <br />

                <strong>Step 2:</strong>
                Begin Transaction.

                <br /><br />

                ↓

                <br />

                <strong>Step 3:</strong>
                Execute SQL statements.

                <br /><br />

                ↓

                <br />

                <strong>Step 4:</strong>
                Check result.

                <br /><br />

                ↓

                <br />

                <strong>If successful:</strong>
                COMMIT Transaction.

                <br /><br />

                <strong>If error occurs:</strong>
                Execute CATCH block.

                <br /><br />

                ↓

                <br />

                ROLLBACK Transaction.

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         COMMIT / ROLLBACK
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                COMMIT and ROLLBACK with TRY...CATCH
            </h2>

            <div class="table-responsive">

                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                    <thead class="table-primary">

                        <tr>

                            <th>Situation</th>

                            <th>Action</th>

                        </tr>

                    </thead>

                    <tbody>

                        <tr>

                            <td>
                                All operations succeed.
                            </td>

                            <td>
                                <strong>COMMIT TRANSACTION</strong>
                            </td>

                        </tr>

                        <tr>

                            <td>
                                An error occurs.
                            </td>

                            <td>
                                <strong>ROLLBACK TRANSACTION</strong>
                            </td>

                        </tr>

                        <tr>

                            <td>
                                Need error details.
                            </td>

                            <td>
                                Use ERROR_* functions.
                            </td>

                        </tr>

                    </tbody>

                </table>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         IMPORTANT POINTS
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Important Points
            </h2>

            <ul>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    TRY contains the statements that may generate an error.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    CATCH handles errors generated inside the TRY block.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    BEGIN TRANSACTION starts the transaction.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    COMMIT TRANSACTION saves successful changes.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    ROLLBACK TRANSACTION undoes uncommitted changes.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    @@TRANCOUNT can be checked before rolling back.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    ERROR_MESSAGE() and other ERROR_* functions can
                    provide information about the error.
                </li>

            </ul>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         SUMMARY
    ========================== -->

    <div class="alert alert-primary shadow-sm mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Summary
        </h2>

        <p>
            Using <strong>TRY...CATCH</strong> with transactions
            provides a structured way to handle database errors.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-0">
            When all operations are successful, the transaction is
            committed. If an error occurs, the CATCH block can roll
            back the transaction and return useful error information.
        </p>

    </div>

